Vita (--vita-fast-particle-palette=off|on, platform/vita/runtime/visual_skips.hpp): off by
default. Dusklight's particle batch never takes child particles: each child is its own draw, one
position matrix loaded into slot 0 and then the quad's display list. In Kakariko that is 135
draws per frame (Vita3K count). The console has ten position-matrix slots and a per-vertex slot
index, the path every skinned model uses. On, an emitter whose children need nothing but their
matrix keeps the matrices back and sends up to ten children at once: matrix k into slot k, then
one display list with the same quads in the same order, each vertex carrying its slot index.
Every vertex is still transformed by its own particle's matrix with the same shader arithmetic;
the colour, texture and blend state are the emitter's, as before. Emitters with a per-child
colour, texture or size call, point or line shapes, a projected texture or a particle callback
keep the one-draw-each path.

